From: aleks2 (H38)
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] idempotent game-mode lifecycle

onGameModeDeactivated() and mod_shutdown() both ran the whole teardown, removeMenuTab() freed its handle without
invalidating it (the host logged "unregister_menu_tab: stale handle"), a failure half way through activation left
the earlier resources acquired, and the preload thread could outlive what it touches.

session_lifecycle.hpp holds the state machine (Inactive / Activating / Active / ShuttingDown) and the resources in
acquisition order: hooks, save observer, texture replacement, UI, seed state, preload thread. A failed activation
rolls back what it acquired in reverse; shutdown() releases each resource exactly once however many times it runs,
preload thread first (cancel flag raised, then joined) so nothing it touches is gone while it runs. Handles are
invalidated as they are freed (release_handle). The UI's menu tab and styles use the same idiom, and a failed
ui::initialize releases its own styles.
